{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNbyzp8g1VJeYBtuubKLhm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor R&D Surface v6 â€” \"Linked Pipeline\" â€” Master Plan (frozen design)\n2\t\n3\t> Crucible Stage 1 output, locked 2026-06-14. Builds on the merged v5 \"Durable\n4\t> Work\" cockpit (close-to-tile vs kill, past-session summary + continue-live, grass\n5\t> B+C workbench, per-build deliverable). v6 comes straight from J.C. Liechty\n6\t> **dogfooding the cockpit** â€” running real researchPrime + Crucible sessions inside\n7\t> the Anchor project window â€” and hitting three concrete walls: sessions don't chain\n8\t> into one another, the session windows aren't real windows, and the summaries +\n9\t> main dashboard are uninformative/broken. v6 makes the trio a **linked, first-class,\n10\t> honestly-summarized pipeline**.\n11\t>\n12\t> Approved interaction mockup: `_mockups/rnd-v6/session_pipeline.html` (the\n13\t> plain-English walkthrough John signed off the decisions against). Build cwd = repo\n14\t> root `C:\\dev\\Anchor`. Each wave ends GREEN on `python -m pytest -v`.\n15\t\n16\t## North Star (locked)\n17\t\n18\tMake the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman trio a **single linked pipeline of\n19\tfirst-class session windows, backed by summaries that are actually true and a main\n20\tdashboard that reflects live project work.** Concretely:\n21\t\n22\t1. **Every session is a first-class window.** A research, planning, or build session\n23\t   opens as a window the user can **minimize, freely resize, and maximize** (plus the\n24\t   v5 close-to-tile and hard-kill). Windows **stack in a column** (not floating).\n25\t2. **Every new session mints a new tile.** Starting a session ALWAYS adds a new tile\n26\t   to the tiles row â€” it never silently reuses or replaces an existing one.\n27\t3. **The trio auto-chains, with the right human-in-the-loop.** A **research** session\n28\t   advances to a **planning** session **on the user's explicit click** (not every\n29\t   research needs planning). A **planning** session advances to a **build** session\n30\t   **automatically â€” but only when that planning session actually produced a\n31\t   Foreman-ready plan** (a Master + Implementation plan set exists); a planning\n32\t   session with no plan simply doesn't advance.\n33\t4. **Same-problem sessions are linked into one traversable chain.** research â†’ planning\n34\t   â†’ build are tied together (durable parent/chain link) and the chain is **visible\n35\t   and clickable** from any of its tiles/windows.\n36\t5. **Finished tiles stay, newest-first.** A finished session keeps its tile; the\n37\t   **newest** session is the prominent tile, older ones collapse into a **\"previously\n38\t   done\"** group â€” nothing vanishes, everything is reopenable.\n39\t6. **Summaries are true and informative.** Session and project summaries actually\n40\t   render real, grounded content (the prod stream-json parse bug is fixed) and convey\n41\t   what the session/project is *for* â€” never blank, never boilerplate, never\n42\t   fabricated.\n43\t7. **The main dashboard reflects project work.** The home dashboard shows, per R&D\n44\t   project, **what's happening now** â€” running sessions, latest progress, the latest\n45\t   grounded summary â€” not just a status dot.\n46\t\n47\t## Why v6 (what's wrong today, from live use)\n48\t\n49\t1. **Sessions are islands.** Running research then planning then build means manually\n50\t   starting three disconnected sessions; nothing carries context forward and nothing\n51\t   records that they're the same effort. The user explicitly wants researchâ†’planâ†’build\n52\t   to flow and stay linked.\n53\t2. **\"Windows\" aren't windows.** The v4.1/v5 inline panels only minimize + close +\n54\t   kill; there is **no maximize and no free resize** (only the terminal sub-pane\n55\t   resizes vertically). The user asked for real minimize/resize/maximize on the\n56\t   session windows.\n57\t3. **Tile behavior is unreliable & lossy in the row.** Starting a new session doesn't\n58\t   always feel like it mints a new tile, and **finished sessions drop out of the\n59\t   top tiles row** (`repopulate()` excludes terminal-status sessions), so the chain\n60\t   you just ran disappears until a reload.\n61\t4. **Summaries are broken in production.** Every real project shows *\"No grounded\n62\t   objective could be extracted\"* and session `summary.md` files are **empty** â€” the\n63\t   summarizer discards 100% of `claude -p --output-format stream-json` output (it\n64\t   skips the very envelope lines that carry the text). Tests passed because the stub\n65\t   emits bare lines: a tested-but-broken-in-prod gap. (Root-cause fix already exists\n66\t   as commit `1bd8b85`; v6 lands it and builds the real-envelope regression guard +\n67\t   content quality on top.)\n68\t5. **The main dashboard ignores R&D activity.** `render` maps a project to a single\n69\t   status dot (\"green if any lane has a running session\"); it does not surface what is\n70\t   running, recent progress, or the latest summary â€” v5's \"timely dashboard\n71\t   reflection\" under-delivered to a dot.\n72\t\n73\t## Locked decisions (Stage 0/1 user gates â€” from John's answers on the mockup)\n74\t\n75\t1. **Window controls = minimize Â· resize Â· maximize Â· close Â· kill, STACKED.** Each\n76\t   session window (research/plan/build) gains **maximize** (fill the cockpit viewport,\n77\t   toggle to restore) and **free resize** (drag any edge/corner) on top of the\n78\t   existing minimize, close-to-tile (keeps the session), and hard-kill. Layout stays\n79\t   the v5 **stacked panel column** â€” NOT floating/draggable windows. (John: \"Stacked\n80\t   is fine for tiles.\")\n81\t2. **New session â‡’ new tile, always.** Every session-start path (`term_start`,\n82\t   continue, advance, promote-grass, grass-develop) mints a distinct tile that appears\n83\t   in the tiles row. No path reuses/replaces a tile. (John: \"when I start a new\n84\t   session/tile then it should show up in the list of tiles.\")\n85\t3. **Research â†’ Planning: MANUAL advance.** A research session's window carries an\n86\t   **\"Advance to Planning â†’\"** control. Clicking it starts a NEW planning session in\n87\t   the same chain, **seeded** from the research (its grounded summary / report), and\n88\t   **linked** to it. Nothing auto-advances research. (John: \"Advance research to\n89\t   planning only on my click â€” some don't advance.\")\n90\t4. **Planning â†’ Build: AUTOMATIC, gated on a real plan.** When a planning session\n91\t   reaches a terminal/**DONE** state â€” the deliberate **hard-kill** (\"I'm done with\n92\t   planning\") or **reconcile-dead** â€” AND a **Foreman-ready plan set** tied to it is\n93\t   discoverable (`handoff.discover_recent_plan_set` finds a MASTER+IMPL pair), the\n94\t   cockpit **automatically** opens a new linked **build** tile, primed via\n95\t   `handoff.prime_worktree` (HANDOFF.md referencing the plan docs) and seeded for\n96\t   Foreman. The build is primed from the discovered plan set **before** the planning\n97\t   worktree is reaped, so the plan docs are never lost. A **keep-alive close does NOT\n98\t   advance** (the session is still live â€” you're not done), and a planning session\n99\t   that produced **no** plan set does **not** advance. This holds even when the\n100\t   planning session had **no upstream research**. (John: \"Advance planning to\n101\t   implementation automatically.\" â€” OPEN UX nuance flagged for John: whether the\n102\t   natural \"I'm done planning\" gesture should be the hard-kill, a dedicated \"Finish â†’\n103\t   Build\" button, or a keep-alive close; v6 ships kill/reconcile-dead as the trigger\n104\t   and a \"Finish â†’ Build\" affordance can be added if John prefers.)\n105\t5. **Linked chain = durable + traversable.** Each session record gains\n106\t   `parent_session_id` and `chain_id`; a chain is research â†’ planning â†’ build (â†’ â€¦).\n107\t   The window/tile shows a **chain breadcrumb** (e.g. `R-1 â†’ P-2 â†’ B-1`) you can click\n108\t   to jump between linked sessions. The link is created at advance/continue/promote\n109\t   time and survives restart + rescan (persisted in the registry + `handoff`/\n110\t   `discovery.json`).\n111\t6. **Finished tiles kept, newest-prominent + \"previously done.\"** Terminal-status\n112\t   sessions remain in the tiles row. Per lane/chain the **most-recent** session is the\n113\t   prominent tile; older finished ones collapse under a **\"previously done\"** group\n114\t   (matching the existing project-window \"most-recent visible + previous-sessions\n115\t   expander\" idiom). Closing never loses a tile; only hard-kill removes one.\n116\t   (John: \"Keep finished tiles â€¦ most recent tile up top â€¦ others moved to previously\n117\t   done.\")\n118\t7. **Summaries fixed + informative + regression-proof.** Land the stream-json parse\n119\t   fix (commit `1bd8b85`: `job_runner.extract_assistant_text` + shared\n120\t   `summarizer._claims_from_job` + `SUMMARY_SCHEMA_VERSION` cache auto-heal +\n121\t   `tests/stub_streamjson.py`/`test_summary_streamjson.py`). On top: strengthen the\n122\t   session + project summary **content** (skill Â· prompts Â· actions for sessions;\n123\t   objective/purpose for projects), keep the generate-twice + grounding filter\n124\t   (honest when absent, never fabricated), and ensure pre-fix empty caches **auto-heal\n125\t   on rescan**. Any test that drives a model through the runner seam MUST use a\n126\t   **stream-json-shaped stub**, not bare lines.\n127\t8. **Main dashboard reflects project activity.** The home dashboard's R&D project\n128\t   rows surface, per project: running-session presence/count, the **latest grounded\n129\t   project summary** (objective), and a **timely \"what's happening\"** line (most-recent\n130\t   lane activity / newest session title). It **reads caches only** on render (no\n131\t   synchronous model call); a background refresh + the existing `projects_html`\n132\t   in-place re-render keep it current.\n133\t9. **Verification standard (non-negotiable, the v4 lesson).** Every UI wave's \"GREEN\"\n134\t   = **rendered-DOM assertions** (positive AND negative) **+ a real Playwright/Chromium\n135\t   interaction test** (click the control, assert the DOM, no JS console errors) **+ an\n136\t   orchestrator screenshot checked against `_mockups/rnd-v6/session_pipeline.html`**\n137\t   **+ the user's sign-off before merge.** A string-grep gate is an automatic HALT.\n138\t10. **Scope = one build** on `C:\\dev\\Anchor`, every wave GREEN on `python -m\n139\t    pytest -v`. Branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v6`; **no merge to master and no service\n140\t    restart without John's sign-off.**\n141\t\n142\t## Out of scope (inclusion test â€” bloat / later)\n143\t\n144\t- **Calendar integration** and the **app-building version of Anchor** â€” explicitly\n145\t  deferred by John for this round.\n146\t- **Floating/draggable windows** â€” rejected in favor of stacked (Decision 1).\n147\t- A full transcript replay/scrubber (the grounded summary suffices), multi-user, and\n148\t  cross-project chain views. Re-architecting the summarizer or terminal substrate â€”\n149\t  v6 **extends** them, never forks.\n150\t- Auto-advancing **researchâ†’plan** (kept manual per Decision 3) and auto-advancing a\n151\t  **plan-less** planning session (Decision 4).\n152\t\n153\t## Hard constraints (from CLAUDE.md â€” non-negotiable)\n154\t\n155\t- **Python stdlib only**, except the declared lazy `pywinpty` (`pty_manager.py` only).\n156\t  **Playwright is a DEV-ONLY test dep** (`pytest.importorskip`), never imported by\n157\t  product code; `distro.py`'s import scan must stay green.\n158\t- **Never bind/touch the live `:8777` service or real data in tests/healthcheck.**\n159\t  Model calls via `tests/fake_claude.py` / stream-json stub through\n160\t  `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`; PTY via the stub backend (`ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`); any\n161\t  spawned preview/service on an OS-assigned port **HARD-guarded `!= 8777`** + isolated\n162\t  temp `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`.\n163\t- **All mutating / terminal / advance endpoints** behind the `do_POST` token gate;\n164\t  GET read-only (token via `?token=`).\n165\t- **f-string brace discipline** in `anchor_gui.py` (`_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` is a RAW\n166\t  single-brace string; doubled braces in f-string HTML/CSS).\n167\t- **Reuse, don't fork:** `terminal_session.py`, `session_registry.py`, `worktrees.py`,\n168\t  `handoff.py`, `summarizer.py`, `effort_history.py`, `job_runner.py`, `pty_manager.py`,\n169\t  `vendor/xterm`. **Mirror** new data seams into `anchor.py`; **extend**\n170\t  `anchor_healthcheck.py` (`check_rnd_v6_surface`, fully stubbed); **update** `CLAUDE.md`.\n171\t- **Scoped commits only** â€” never sweep runtime-data churn (`dashboard.html`,\n172\t  `PROJECTS.md`, `DASHBOARD.md`, `domains/*`, `INBOX.md`, `.anchor/`, `rnd_jobs/`,\n173\t  `rnd_registry.json`, `logs/`). Commit only the code/test files each wave touches.\n174\t\n175\t## Risks & mitigations\n176\t\n177\t- **R1 â€” auto planâ†’build fires wrongly / spawns junk builds.** Gate strictly on\n178\t  `discover_recent_plan_set` returning a real MASTER+IMPL pair tied to that planning\n179\t  session; no plan set â‡’ no advance. Make the trigger **idempotent** (one build per\n180\t  planning session â€” keyed by `parent_session_id`) so reconcile/restart can't spawn\n181\t  duplicates. Surface it as a clearly-attributed new tile, never silently. Test: a\n182\t  planning session with a plan set auto-opens exactly one linked primed build; a\n183\t  plan-less one opens none; re-running reconcile doesn't duplicate.\n184\t- **R2 â€” \"automatic\" never fires because interactive sessions don't exit.** Define the\n185\t  trigger on the planning session reaching a terminal/**DONE** state via the deliberate\n186\t  **hard-kill** (\"done with planning\") or **reconcile-dead** â€” NOT on a keep-alive\n187\t  close (which leaves it running, v5) and NOT on process self-exit. **Prime the build\n188\t  from the discovered plan set BEFORE the planning worktree is reaped** so the plan\n189\t  docs survive. Test the kill/reconcile-dead transition drives exactly one advance and\n190\t  the build's HANDOFF.md references the real plan docs.\n191\t- **R3 â€” chain links break on restart/rescan.** Persist `parent_session_id`/`chain_id`\n192\t  in the registry record (survives restart) AND mirror the cross-lane edge into\n193\t  `handoff`/`discovery.json` (rescan-durable, like v3 handoffs). Test: a chain survives\n194\t  a registry reload + a rescan.\n195\t- **R4 â€” keeping finished tiles re-clutters / re-introduces the v3 stale-session\n196\t  problem.** Newest-prominent + \"previously done\" collapse bounds the visible set;\n197\t  reconcile still re-statuses dead sessions; closing keeps the record, only kill\n198\t  reaps. Test: N finished sessions render one prominent + a collapsed group; kill\n199\t  removes; reopen works.\n200\t- **R5 â€” summary still blank / fabricated in prod.** The parse fix + a **stream-json\n201\t  shaped** regression stub (not bare lines) + the generate-twice + grounding filter +\n202\t  `SUMMARY_SCHEMA_VERSION` auto-heal. Honest placeholder when truly absent. Test:\n203\t  realistic stream-json yields a grounded non-empty summary; an ungrounded claim is\n204\t  dropped; a pre-fix empty cache heals on rescan.\n205\t- **R6 â€” another vacuous UI gate ships a broken UI.** Decision 9 (DOM + Playwright +\n206\t  screenshot + sign-off) mandatory per UI wave; a string-grep gate HALTs the wave.\n207\t- **R7 â€” window resize/maximize fights the xterm fit + terminal pump.** Reuse the v4.1\n208\t  proven fit/resize-observer; maximize/restore must re-fit the terminal; assert no\n209\t  freeze + correct cols/rows after resize. Test in the Playwright wave.\n210\t\n211\t## Definition of done (project)\n212\t\n213\tAll waves GREEN on `python -m pytest -v` AND: each session window minimizes / freely\n214\tresizes / maximizes / closes-to-tile / hard-kills, stacked; every new session mints a\n215\tnew tile; a research window's \"Advance to Planning â†’\" starts a linked, seeded planning\n216\tsession; a planning session that produced a plan set **auto-opens** a linked, primed\n217\tbuild tile (and a plan-less one does not), even with no upstream research; sessions of\n218\tone problem form a durable, traversable researchâ†’planâ†’build chain with a breadcrumb;\n219\tfinished tiles persist newest-prominent with a \"previously done\" group; session +\n220\tproject summaries render real grounded content via the stream-json fix (regression-\n221\tguarded, honest when absent); the main dashboard reflects per-project running/progress/\n222\tsummary from cache; the CLI mirrors the new read seams; `check_rnd_v6_surface` passes\n223\tfully stubbed (no `:8777`, no orphans); `distro` scan clean (no Playwright in product\n224\tcode); `CLAUDE.md` updated; and **every UI wave is verified by Playwright + a\n225\tscreenshot + John's sign-off before merge.**\n226\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"594fe9ce-c57e-43ec-93aa-7b0ba81bfc73","uuid":"81877ba9-6a8a-41cf-9bec-d81ccd6391a6","timestamp":"2026-06-15T12:19:01.123Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\planning\\rnd-v6\\MASTER-PLAN.md","content":"# Anchor R&D Surface v6 â€” \"Linked Pipeline\" â€” Master Plan (frozen design)\n\n> Crucible Stage 1 output, locked 2026-06-14. Builds on the merged v5 \"Durable\n> Work\" cockpit (close-to-tile vs kill, past-session summary + continue-live, grass\n> B+C workbench, per-build deliverable). v6 comes straight from J.C. Liechty\n> **dogfooding the cockpit** â€” running real researchPrime + Crucible sessions inside\n> the Anchor project window â€” and hitting three concrete walls: sessions don't chain\n> into one another, the session windows aren't real windows, and the summaries +\n> main dashboard are uninformative/broken. v6 makes the trio a **linked, first-class,\n> honestly-summarized pipeline**.\n>\n> Approved interaction mockup: `_mockups/rnd-v6/session_pipeline.html` (the\n> plain-English walkthrough John signed off the decisions against). Build cwd = repo\n> root `C:\\dev\\Anchor`. Each wave ends GREEN on `python -m pytest -v`.\n\n## North Star (locked)\n\nMake the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman trio a **single linked pipeline of\nfirst-class session windows, backed by summaries that are actually true and a main\ndashboard that reflects live project work.** Concretely:\n\n1. **Every session is a first-class window.** A research, planning, or build session\n   opens as a window the user can **minimize, freely resize, and maximize** (plus the\n   v5 close-to-tile and hard-kill). Windows **stack in a column** (not floating).\n2. **Every new session mints a new tile.** Starting a session ALWAYS adds a new tile\n   to the tiles row â€” it never silently reuses or replaces an existing one.\n3. **The trio auto-chains, with the right human-in-the-loop.** A **research** session\n   advances to a **planning** session **on the user's explicit click** (not every\n   research needs planning). A **planning** session advances to a **build** session\n   **automatically â€” but only when that planning session actually produced a\n   Foreman-ready plan** (a Master + Implementation plan set exists); a planning\n   session with no plan simply doesn't advance.\n4. **Same-problem sessions are linked into one traversable chain.** research â†’ planning\n   â†’ build are tied together (durable parent/chain link) and the chain is **visible\n   and clickable** from any of its tiles/windows.\n5. **Finished tiles stay, newest-first.** A finished session keeps its tile; the\n   **newest** session is the prominent tile, older ones collapse into a **\"previously\n   done\"** group â€” nothing vanishes, everything is reopenable.\n6. **Summaries are true and informative.** Session and project summaries actually\n   render real, grounded content (the prod stream-json parse bug is fixed) and convey\n   what the session/project is *for* â€” never blank, never boilerplate, never\n   fabricated.\n7. **The main dashboard reflects project work.** The home dashboard shows, per R&D\n   project, **what's happening now** â€” running sessions, latest progress, the latest\n   grounded summary â€” not just a status dot.\n\n## Why v6 (what's wrong today, from live use)\n\n1. **Sessions are islands.** Running research then planning then build means manually\n   starting three disconnected sessions; nothing carries context forward and nothing\n   records that they're the same effort. The user explicitly wants researchâ†’planâ†’build\n   to flow and stay linked.\n2. **\"Windows\" aren't windows.** The v4.1/v5 inline panels only minimize + close +\n   kill; there is **no maximize and no free resize** (only the terminal sub-pane\n   resizes vertically). The user asked for real minimize/resize/maximize on the\n   session windows.\n3. **Tile behavior is unreliable & lossy in the row.** Starting a new session doesn't\n   always feel like it mints a new tile, and **finished sessions drop out of the\n   top tiles row** (`repopulate()` excludes terminal-status sessions), so the chain\n   you just ran disappears until a reload.\n4. **Summaries are broken in production.** Every real project shows *\"No grounded\n   objective could be extracted\"* and session `summary.md` files are **empty** â€” the\n   summarizer discards 100% of `claude -p --output-format stream-json` output (it\n   skips the very envelope lines that carry the text). Tests passed because the stub\n   emits bare lines: a tested-but-broken-in-prod gap. (Root-cause fix already exists\n   as commit `1bd8b85`; v6 lands it and builds the real-envelope regression guard +\n   content quality on top.)\n5. **The main dashboard ignores R&D activity.** `render` maps a project to a single\n   status dot (\"green if any lane has a running session\"); it does not surface what is\n   running, recent progress, or the latest summary â€” v5's \"timely dashboard\n   reflection\" under-delivered to a dot.\n\n## Locked decisions (Stage 0/1 user gates â€” from John's answers on the mockup)\n\n1. **Window controls = minimize Â· resize Â· maximize Â· close Â· kill, STACKED.** Each\n   session window (research/plan/build) gains **maximize** (fill the cockpit viewport,\n   toggle to restore) and **free resize** (drag any edge/corner) on top of the\n   existing minimize, close-to-tile (keeps the session), and hard-kill. Layout stays\n   the v5 **stacked panel column** â€” NOT floating/draggable windows. (John: \"Stacked\n   is fine for tiles.\")\n2. **New session â‡’ new tile, always.** Every session-start path (`term_start`,\n   continue, advance, promote-grass, grass-develop) mints a distinct tile that appears\n   in the tiles row. No path reuses/replaces a tile. (John: \"when I start a new\n   session/tile then it should show up in the list of tiles.\")\n3. **Research â†’ Planning: MANUAL advance.** A research session's window carries an\n   **\"Advance to Planning â†’\"** control. Clicking it starts a NEW planning session in\n   the same chain, **seeded** from the research (its grounded summary / report), and\n   **linked** to it. Nothing auto-advances research. (John: \"Advance research to\n   planning only on my click â€” some don't advance.\")\n4. **Planning â†’ Build: AUTOMATIC, gated on a real plan.** When a planning session\n   reaches a terminal/**DONE** state â€” the deliberate **hard-kill** (\"I'm done with\n   planning\") or **reconcile-dead** â€” AND a **Foreman-ready plan set** tied to it is\n   discoverable (`handoff.discover_recent_plan_set` finds a MASTER+IMPL pair), the\n   cockpit **automatically** opens a new linked **build** tile, primed via\n   `handoff.prime_worktree` (HANDOFF.md referencing the plan docs) and seeded for\n   Foreman. The build is primed from the discovered plan set **before** the planning\n   worktree is reaped, so the plan docs are never lost. A **keep-alive close does NOT\n   advance** (the session is still live â€” you're not done), and a planning session\n   that produced **no** plan set does **not** advance. This holds even when the\n   planning session had **no upstream research**. (John: \"Advance planning to\n   implementation automatically.\" â€” OPEN UX nuance flagged for John: whether the\n   natural \"I'm done planning\" gesture should be the hard-kill, a dedicated \"Finish â†’\n   Build\" button, or a keep-alive close; v6 ships kill/reconcile-dead as the trigger\n   and a \"Finish â†’ Build\" affordance can be added if John prefers.)\n5. **Linked chain = durable + traversable.** Each session record gains\n   `parent_session_id` and `chain_id`; a chain is research â†’ planning â†’ build (â†’ â€¦).\n   The window/tile shows a **chain breadcrumb** (e.g. `R-1 â†’ P-2 â†’ B-1`) you can click\n   to jump between linked sessions. The link is created at advance/continue/promote\n   time and survives restart + rescan (persisted in the registry + `handoff`/\n   `discovery.json`).\n6. **Finished tiles kept, newest-prominent + \"previously done.\"** Terminal-status\n   sessions remain in the tiles row. Per lane/chain the **most-recent** session is the\n   prominent tile; older finished ones collapse under a **\"previously done\"** group\n   (matching the existing project-window \"most-recent visible + previous-sessions\n   expander\" idiom). Closing never loses a tile; only hard-kill removes one.\n   (John: \"Keep finished tiles â€¦ most recent tile up top â€¦ others moved to previously\n   done.\")\n7. **Summaries fixed + informative + regression-proof.** Land the stream-json parse\n   fix (commit `1bd8b85`: `job_runner.extract_assistant_text` + shared\n   `summarizer._claims_from_job` + `SUMMARY_SCHEMA_VERSION` cache auto-heal +\n   `tests/stub_streamjson.py`/`test_summary_streamjson.py`). On top: strengthen the\n   session + project summary **content** (skill Â· prompts Â· actions for sessions;\n   objective/purpose for projects), keep the generate-twice + grounding filter\n   (honest when absent, never fabricated), and ensure pre-fix empty caches **auto-heal\n   on rescan**. Any test that drives a model through the runner seam MUST use a\n   **stream-json-shaped stub**, not bare lines.\n8. **Main dashboard reflects project activity.** The home dashboard's R&D project\n   rows surface, per project: running-session presence/count, the **latest grounded\n   project summary** (objective), and a **timely \"what's happening\"** line (most-recent\n   lane activity / newest session title). It **reads caches only** on render (no\n   synchronous model call); a background refresh + the existing `projects_html`\n   in-place re-render keep it current.\n9. **Verification standard (non-negotiable, the v4 lesson).** Every UI wave's \"GREEN\"\n   = **rendered-DOM assertions** (positive AND negative) **+ a real Playwright/Chromium\n   interaction test** (click the control, assert the DOM, no JS console errors) **+ an\n   orchestrator screenshot checked against `_mockups/rnd-v6/session_pipeline.html`**\n   **+ the user's sign-off before merge.** A string-grep gate is an automatic HALT.\n10. **Scope = one build** on `C:\\dev\\Anchor`, every wave GREEN on `python -m\n    pytest -v`. Branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v6`; **no merge to master and no service\n    restart without John's sign-off.**\n\n## Out of scope (inclusion test â€” bloat / later)\n\n- **Calendar integration** and the **app-building version of Anchor** â€” explicitly\n  deferred by John for this round.\n- **Floating/draggable windows** â€” rejected in favor of stacked (Decision 1).\n- A full transcript replay/scrubber (the grounded summary suffices), multi-user, and\n  cross-project chain views. Re-architecting the summarizer or terminal substrate â€”\n  v6 **extends** them, never forks.\n- Auto-advancing **researchâ†’plan** (kept manual per Decision 3) and auto-advancing a\n  **plan-less** planning session (Decision 4).\n\n## Hard constraints (from CLAUDE.md â€” non-negotiable)\n\n- **Python stdlib only**, except the declared lazy `pywinpty` (`pty_manager.py` only).\n  **Playwright is a DEV-ONLY test dep** (`pytest.importorskip`), never imported by\n  product code; `distro.py`'s import scan must stay green.\n- **Never bind/touch the live `:8777` service or real data in tests/healthcheck.**\n  Model calls via `tests/fake_claude.py` / stream-json stub through\n  `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`; PTY via the stub backend (`ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`); any\n  spawned preview/service on an OS-assigned port **HARD-guarded `!= 8777`** + isolated\n  temp `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`.\n- **All mutating / terminal / advance endpoints** behind the `do_POST` token gate;\n  GET read-only (token via `?token=`).\n- **f-string brace discipline** in `anchor_gui.py` (`_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` is a RAW\n  single-brace string; doubled braces in f-string HTML/CSS).\n- **Reuse, don't fork:** `terminal_session.py`, `session_registry.py`, `worktrees.py`,\n  `handoff.py`, `summarizer.py`, `effort_history.py`, `job_runner.py`, `pty_manager.py`,\n  `vendor/xterm`. **Mirror** new data seams into `anchor.py`; **extend**\n  `anchor_healthcheck.py` (`check_rnd_v6_surface`, fully stubbed); **update** `CLAUDE.md`.\n- **Scoped commits only** â€” never sweep runtime-data churn (`dashboard.html`,\n  `PROJECTS.md`, `DASHBOARD.md`, `domains/*`, `INBOX.md`, `.anchor/`, `rnd_jobs/`,\n  `rnd_registry.json`, `logs/`). Commit only the code/test files each wave touches.\n\n## Risks & mitigations\n\n- **R1 â€” auto planâ†’build fires wrongly / spawns junk builds.** Gate strictly on\n  `discover_recent_plan_set` returning a real MASTER+IMPL pair tied to that planning\n  session; no plan set â‡’ no advance. Make the trigger **idempotent** (one build per\n  planning session â€” keyed by `parent_session_id`) so reconcile/restart can't spawn\n  duplicates. Surface it as a clearly-attributed new tile, never silently. Test: a\n  planning session with a plan set auto-opens exactly one linked primed build; a\n  plan-less one opens none; re-running reconcile doesn't duplicate.\n- **R2 â€” \"automatic\" never fires because interactive sessions don't exit.** Define the\n  trigger on the planning session reaching a terminal/**DONE** state via the deliberate\n  **hard-kill** (\"done with planning\") or **reconcile-dead** â€” NOT on a keep-alive\n  close (which leaves it running, v5) and NOT on process self-exit. **Prime the build\n  from the discovered plan set BEFORE the planning worktree is reaped** so the plan\n  docs survive. Test the kill/reconcile-dead transition drives exactly one advance and\n  the build's HANDOFF.md references the real plan docs.\n- **R3 â€” chain links break on restart/rescan.** Persist `parent_session_id`/`chain_id`\n  in the registry record (survives restart) AND mirror the cross-lane edge into\n  `handoff`/`discovery.json` (rescan-durable, like v3 handoffs). Test: a chain survives\n  a registry reload + a rescan.\n- **R4 â€” keeping finished tiles re-clutters / re-introduces the v3 stale-session\n  problem.** Newest-prominent + \"previously done\" collapse bounds the visible set;\n  reconcile still re-statuses dead sessions; closing keeps the record, only kill\n  reaps. Test: N finished sessions render one prominent + a collapsed group; kill\n  removes; reopen works.\n- **R5 â€” summary still blank / fabricated in prod.** The parse fix + a **stream-json\n  shaped** regression stub (not bare lines) + the generate-twice + grounding filter +\n  `SUMMARY_SCHEMA_VERSION` auto-heal. Honest placeholder when truly absent. Test:\n  realistic stream-json yields a grounded non-empty summary; an ungrounded claim is\n  dropped; a pre-fix empty cache heals on rescan.\n- **R6 â€” another vacuous UI gate ships a broken UI.** Decision 9 (DOM + Playwright +\n  screenshot + sign-off) mandatory per UI wave; a string-grep gate HALTs the wave.\n- **R7 â€” window resize/maximize fights the xterm fit + terminal pump.** Reuse the v4.1\n  proven fit/resize-observer; maximize/restore must re-fit the terminal; assert no\n  freeze + correct cols/rows after resize. Test in the Playwright wave.\n\n## Definition of done (project)\n\nAll waves GREEN on `python -m pytest -v` AND: each session window minimizes / freely\nresizes / maximizes / closes-to-tile / hard-kills, stacked; every new session mints a\nnew tile; a research window's \"Advance to Planning â†’\" starts a linked, seeded planning\nsession; a planning session that produced a plan set **auto-opens** a linked, primed\nbuild tile (and a plan-less one does not), even with no upstream research; sessions of\none problem form a durable, traversable researchâ†’planâ†’build chain with a breadcrumb;\nfinished tiles persist newest-prominent with a \"previously done\" group; session +\nproject summaries render real grounded content via the stream-json fix (regression-\nguarded, honest when absent); the main dashboard reflects per-project running/progress/\nsummary from cache; the CLI mirrors the new read seams; `check_rnd_v6_surface` passes\nfully stubbed (no `:8777`, no orphans); `distro` scan clean (no Playwright in product\ncode); `CLAUDE.md` updated; and **every UI wave is verified by Playwright + a\nscreenshot + John's sign-off before merge.**\n","numLines":226,"startLine":1,"totalLines":226}}}
