{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013YAuyJsZ2DjqsPxXTpte3Q","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor R&D Surface v6 â€” \"Linked Pipeline\" â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n2\t\n3\t> Crucible Stage 2 output, locked 2026-06-14. Frozen design: `MASTER-PLAN.md` (this\n4\t> folder) + the approved interaction mockup `_mockups/rnd-v6/session_pipeline.html`.\n5\t> Build cwd = repo root `C:\\dev\\Anchor`, branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v6` (off master;\n6\t> the summarizer parse fix `1bd8b85` is already cherry-picked as the branch base).\n7\t> Each wave ends GREEN on the ground-truth gate and adds/extends tests under `tests/`.\n8\t\n9\ttest-command: python -m pytest -v\n10\t\n11\t## Conventions (read before any wave)\n12\t\n13\t- **Active Anchor project id:** read from `rnd_registry.json` at build time; never\n14\t  hard-code (`2fe37f39â€¦` is retired; the live Anchor is the active one).\n15\t- **No live `claude`/`gemini`/real-PTY in the gate.** Model calls via\n16\t  `tests/fake_claude.py` / `tests/stub_streamjson.py` through `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`;\n17\t  PTY via the stub backend (`ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`). Never `:8777` or real data;\n18\t  any spawned preview/service on an OS-assigned port HARD-guarded `!= 8777` + isolated\n19\t  temp `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`.\n20\t- **pywinpty** is the only native dep (lazy, `pty_manager.py` only). **Playwright is a\n21\t  DEV-ONLY test dep** â€” `pytest.importorskip(\"playwright.sync_api\")`; NEVER in product\n22\t  code; `distro.py`'s scan must stay green (Wave 8 asserts it).\n23\t- **f-string discipline** in `anchor_gui.py`: `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` is a RAW\n24\t  single-brace string; double literal braces in f-string HTML/CSS.\n25\t- **Security:** every new mutating / terminal / advance endpoint behind the existing\n26\t  `do_POST` token gate; GET read-only (token via `?token=`).\n27\t- **Reuse, don't fork:** build on `terminal_session.py`, `session_registry.py`,\n28\t  `worktrees.py`, `handoff.py`, `summarizer.py`, `effort_history.py`, `job_runner.py`,\n29\t  `pty_manager.py`, `report_viewer.py`, `vendor/xterm`.\n30\t- **Scoped commits only** â€” never the runtime-data churn (`dashboard.html`,\n31\t  `PROJECTS.md`, `DASHBOARD.md`, `domains/*`, `INBOX.md`, `.anchor/`, `rnd_jobs/`,\n32\t  `rnd_registry.json`, `logs/`). Commit only the code/test files each wave touched.\n33\t- **Baseline before Wave 1:** the v5 merge baseline was **643 passed, 1 skipped**;\n34\t  the cherry-picked summarizer fix adds `tests/test_summary_streamjson.py`\n35\t  (+ stub). Re-establish the live count at Wave 1 start; each wave must hold or grow it.\n36\t- **UI VERIFICATION IS MANDATORY (the v4 lesson â€” non-negotiable)** for every wave\n37\t  that changes rendered UI (Waves 3, 4, 5, 6, 7). \"GREEN\" requires ALL of: (a)\n38\t  **rendered-DOM assertions** â€” parse the served HTML (style/script stripped) with\n39\t  `html.parser`, assert the new structure present AND the replaced/old structure\n40\t  absent (positive + negative); (b) a **real Playwright + Chromium interaction test**\n41\t  (boot a throwaway `gui.make_server('127.0.0.1',0)`, click the actual control, assert\n42\t  the resulting DOM + no JS console errors) â€” model on `tests/test_cockpit_paradigm2.py`\n43\t  / `tests/test_run_lifecycle.py`; (c) the **orchestrator captures a screenshot**\n44\t  (PNG under `_devtest/`), **Reads it**, and checks it against the rnd-v6 mockup; (d)\n45\t  **user sign-off before merge**. A string-grep-only test is an automatic wave HALT.\n46\t\n47\t---\n48\t\n49\t## Wave 1 â€” Summaries that actually work (backend; lands the prod fix + content + heal)\n50\t\n51\tThe parse fix (`1bd8b85`) is already the branch base. This wave makes summaries\n52\tgenuinely *informative* and *regression-proof*, and heals stale caches. Verify\n53\t`summarizer.summarize_session` and `summarize_project` produce grounded, non-empty\n54\tcontent when driven through a **stream-json-shaped** stub (`tests/stub_streamjson.py`),\n55\tnot bare lines. Strengthen the **session** summary to convey skill Â· prompts/turns Â·\n56\tactions/files and the **project** summary to convey objective/purpose (stronger seed:\n57\tCLAUDE.md/README/Anchor.md + newest plan docs + pinned deliverables + per-lane\n58\tactivity). Keep generate-twice + grounding filter (honest \"no grounded â€¦\" only when\n59\ttruly absent; never fabricated). Ensure pre-fix caches (`SUMMARY_SCHEMA_VERSION` older/\n60\tmissing) are treated as a MISS and **regenerate on rescan/force**. Add a small\n61\t`rescan`-path helper (or confirm the existing background `summarize_project` on\n62\t`rescan`) so existing empty project caches heal without manual force.\n63\t\n64\t- **Done-when:** `pytest` GREEN; through the stream-json stub, a session summary is\n65\t  non-empty and carries skill/prompts/actions, and a project summary is a grounded\n66\t  1â€“2 sentence objective; an ungrounded claim is dropped; a `SCHEMA_VERSION`-stale\n67\t  empty cache is regenerated on rescan; bare-line stub back-compat still parses.\n68\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** a session/project whose runner emits `claude --output-format\n69\t  stream-json` envelopes, **When** the summarizer runs through the stub, **Then** it\n70\t  extracts the real text and caches a grounded, non-empty, informative summary;\n71\t  **Given** a pre-fix empty `project-summary.json` (old/again missing schema version),\n72\t  **When** the project is rescanned, **Then** the cache is treated as a miss and\n73\t  regenerated (no longer \"No grounded objective\").\n74\t- **Tests:** extend `tests/test_summary_streamjson.py`; add\n75\t  `tests/test_summary_content_v6.py` (session skill/prompts/actions shape; project\n76\t  objective shape; grounding drops a hallucinated claim; schema-version heal on\n77\t  rescan). Backend only â€” no Playwright unless markup changes.\n78\t\n79\t## Wave 2 â€” Session linkage backbone (backend; the durable chain)\n80\t\n81\tGive sessions a durable lineage. Add `parent_session_id` (str|\"\") and `chain_id` (str)\n82\tto the `session_registry` record (`_normalize` defaults + `register_session` params +\n83\t`update_session` allow-list); a new session with no parent **starts its own chain**\n84\t(`chain_id = session_id`), a child **inherits its parent's `chain_id`**. Add\n85\t`session_registry.chain_for(session_id)` / `chain_members(chain_id)` (ordered\n86\tresearchâ†’planâ†’build by lane then created_at) and a `terminal_session.start_session(...,\n87\tparent_session_id=None)` passthrough that sets both fields. Extend `handoff.py` to\n88\trecord a **generic stage edge** (not just planâ†’build): a `record_stage_link(folder,\n89\tpid, from_session, to_session, kind)` appended to `discovery.json` (rescan-durable via\n90\t`anchor_marker` merge, like existing handoffs), and have `discover_recent_plan_set`\n91\thonor an explicit `source_session_id` already (it does). No UI in this wave.\n92\t\n93\t- **Done-when:** `pytest` GREEN; a child session created with `parent_session_id`\n94\t  inherits the parent's `chain_id`; `chain_members` returns the ordered chain; the\n95\t  stage edge is persisted and **survives a registry reload + a rescan**; existing\n96\t  records (no new fields) normalize with empty parent / self `chain_id` (back-compat).\n97\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** a research session R, **When** a planning session P is started\n98\t  with `parent_session_id=R`, **Then** P.chain_id == R.chain_id and\n99\t  `chain_members(R.chain_id) == [R, P]` ordered; **When** the registry is reloaded and\n100\t  the project rescanned, **Then** the Râ†’P edge and chain still resolve.\n101\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_session_chain.py` â€” field defaults/back-compat; chain\n102\t  inherit + ordering; `chain_for`/`chain_members`; stage-edge persistence across\n103\t  reload + rescan; `start_session(parent_session_id=â€¦)` through the stub PTY.\n104\t\n105\t## Wave 3 â€” First-class session windows: maximize + free resize (UI)\n106\t\n107\tIn `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` + the panel CSS: add a **maximize** control (â–¢) to each panel\n108\theader that toggles the panel to fill the cockpit viewport (`.panel.maxd`) and back,\n109\tand make the panel **freely resizable** (drag any edge/corner â€” not just the terminal\n110\tsub-pane), persisting size per session (extend `_panelHeights` â†’ `_panelRects`).\n111\tKeep the v5 minimize, close-to-tile, and hard-kill exactly as they are; layout stays\n112\tthe **stacked** column. Maximize/restore and resize MUST re-fit the xterm terminal\n113\t(reuse the v4.1 fit + ResizeObserver) with no freeze and correct cols/rows.\n114\t\n115\t- **Done-when:** UI-verification set passes â€” every session panel has working\n116\t  minimize / **maximize (toggle)** / **free resize** / close / kill; maximizing fills\n117\t  the viewport and restores; resizing re-fits the terminal (correct cols/rows, no\n118\t  freeze); the old \"terminal-pane-only vertical resize\" is no longer the only resize.\n119\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** an open session panel, **When** the user clicks maximize,\n120\t  **Then** the panel fills the cockpit and the terminal re-fits; **When** clicked\n121\t  again, **Then** it restores to its prior rect; **When** the user drags the panel's\n122\t  corner, **Then** the panel resizes and the terminal re-fits with no console error.\n123\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_window_controls_v6.py` â€” DOM (maximize control present on\n124\t  panels; resize affordance present; positive+negative vs the v5 header) + Playwright\n125\t  (open panel â†’ maximize â†’ assert maxd geometry + terminal fit â†’ restore â†’ resize\n126\t  drag â†’ assert new size, no JS console errors) + screenshot vs mockup Step 2.\n127\t\n128\t## Wave 4 â€” Tile lifecycle: new-session=new-tile + keep finished (newest-prominent) (UI)\n129\t\n130\tTwo fixes. (a) **Every start mints a tile:** audit every session-start front-end path\n131\t(`newTermSession`, `continueSession`, `promoteGrass`, `developGrass`, and the new\n132\tadvance paths) so each appends a distinct tile to the tiles row â€” none reuse/replace.\n133\t(b) **Keep finished tiles, newest-prominent:** stop excluding terminal-status sessions\n134\tfrom the tiles row (`repopulate`/`renderSessionBar` + the server `term_sessions`\n135\tprojection) so done/failed sessions remain as **greyed, reopenable** tiles; per\n136\tlane/chain render the **most-recent** session as the prominent tile and collapse older\n137\tfinished ones under a **\"previously done\"** group/expander. Reopening a finished tile\n138\tshows its summary panel (Wave 1); closing keeps the tile (v5); only hard-kill removes\n139\tit.\n140\t\n141\t- **Done-when:** UI-verification set passes â€” starting any kind of session adds a new\n142\t  tile; finishing a session keeps its tile (greyed) in the row without a reload; per\n143\t  lane the newest is prominent and older finished ones are under \"previously done\";\n144\t  reopening a finished tile opens its summary; kill removes the tile.\n145\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** the tiles row, **When** the user starts a second research\n146\t  session, **Then** a second distinct research tile appears (the first is not\n147\t  replaced); **When** a session finishes, **Then** its tile remains (greyed) and, if a\n148\t  newer one exists in its lane, moves under \"previously done\"; **When** a finished tile\n149\t  is clicked, **Then** its summary panel opens.\n150\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_tile_lifecycle_v6.py` â€” DOM (multiple same-lane tiles;\n151\t  finished tile present + \"previously done\" group; positive+negative) + Playwright\n152\t  (start two sessions â†’ two tiles; finish one â†’ still present + grouped; reopen â†’\n153\t  summary) + backend (term_sessions projection now includes terminal sessions, still\n154\t  SAFE â€” no worktree_path/branch).\n155\t\n156\t## Wave 5 â€” Manual advance researchâ†’planning + chain breadcrumb (UI + endpoint)\n157\t\n158\tAdd an **\"Advance to Planning â†’\"** control to a research session's window (shown when\n159\tthe session looks done / on demand). It calls a new **`POST /api/rnd/advance_session`**\n160\t(token-authed) â†’ `terminal_session.start_session(lane='planning',\n161\tparent_session_id=<research>, seed_context=<research summary/report>)`, creating a NEW\n162\tlinked planning tile seeded from the research; the research record is never mutated\n163\t(reuses the v5 continue-seed builder). Render a **chain breadcrumb** (`R-1 â†’ P-2 â†’ â€¦`)\n164\tin each session window header (and as a small affordance on the tile) from\n165\t`chain_members`; clicking a breadcrumb node opens that session's panel. (This wave\n166\testablishes the generic advance endpoint that Wave 6 reuses for the auto path.)\n167\t\n168\t- **Done-when:** UI-verification set passes â€” a research window shows \"Advance to\n169\t  Planning â†’\"; clicking it opens a new planning tile in the same chain, seeded from the\n170\t  research, original intact; every linked session shows the chain breadcrumb and\n171\t  clicking a node navigates the chain.\n172\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** a research session with a grounded summary, **When** the user\n173\t  clicks \"Advance to Planning â†’\", **Then** a new RUNNING planning session starts in the\n174\t  same `chain_id` with `parent_session_id` = the research and a seed containing the\n175\t  research context, and the research record is unchanged; **When** the user clicks the\n176\t  breadcrumb's research node from the planning window, **Then** the research panel opens.\n177\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_advance_research_to_plan.py` â€” endpoint auth + seeded-linked\n178\t  start (new session, original intact, chain set) + DOM (advance control on research\n179\t  only; breadcrumb present) + Playwright (click advance â†’ new planning tile + seed;\n180\t  click breadcrumb â†’ navigates) + screenshot vs mockup Step 3.\n181\t\n182\t## Wave 6 â€” Auto advance planningâ†’build (gated on a real plan) (backend + UI)\n183\t\n184\tWhen a **planning** session reaches a terminal/**DONE** state â€” the deliberate\n185\t**hard-kill** (\"done with planning\") or **reconcile-dead**, NOT a keep-alive close â€”\n186\tthe server checks `handoff.discover_recent_plan_set(folder, pid,\n187\tsource_session_id=<planning session>)`. If a **MASTER+IMPL plan set** is found, it\n188\t**automatically** starts a NEW linked **build** session (`start_session(lane='build',\n189\tparent_session_id=<planning>, â€¦)`), **primes** its worktree via\n190\t`handoff.prime_worktree` (HANDOFF.md â†’ the plan docs) **before the planning worktree\n191\tis reaped** (so the plan docs survive), and **records the stage edge** (Wave 2) â€”\n192\texactly one build per planning session (**idempotent** on `parent_session_id`, so\n193\treconcile/restart never duplicates). If **no** plan set is found, **no** advance. The\n194\tnew build tile appears in the row (Wave 4), clearly attributed, even when the planning\n195\tsession had no upstream research. Surface a tiny \"â†’ auto-opened Build B-n from this\n196\tplan\" note. The trigger is the kill/reconcile-dead transition the cockpit already\n197\towns â€” never process self-exit, never a keep-alive close.\n198\t\n199\t- **Done-when:** UI-verification set passes â€” finishing a planning session that\n200\t  produced a plan set auto-opens exactly one linked, primed build tile; a planning\n201\t  session with no plan set opens none; the build is linked into the chain and survives\n202\t  reconcile/restart without duplication; works with no upstream research.\n203\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** a planning session whose worktree contains a MASTER+IMPL plan\n204\t  set, **When** it is hard-killed / found reconcile-dead (DONE transition), **Then**\n205\t  the cockpit opens one build session with `parent_session_id` = the planning session,\n206\t  a primed HANDOFF.md (referencing the real plan docs, captured before reap), and a\n207\t  recorded stage edge; **Given** a planning session with no plan set, **When** it\n208\t  finishes, **Then** no build is opened; **When** reconcile runs again, **Then** no\n209\t  duplicate build is created; **When** a planning panel is keep-alive **closed**,\n210\t  **Then** no build is opened (still live).\n211\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_auto_advance_plan_to_build.py` â€” terminal-transition trigger\n212\t  (stub PTY, temp git project with/without a plan set) â†’ exactly-one primed linked\n213\t  build; idempotency across a second reconcile; no-plan â‡’ no-advance; no upstream\n214\t  research path + DOM/Playwright (finishing a planning panel surfaces the new build\n215\t  tile + note).\n216\t\n217\t## Wave 7 â€” Main dashboard reflects project activity (UI)\n218\t\n219\tUpgrade the home-dashboard R&D project rows (`render_project_tile_html` / the rows\n220\tre-rendered by `GET /api/rnd/projects_html`) from a bare status dot to a **timely\n221\treflection**: per project show running-session presence/count, the **latest grounded\n222\tproject summary** (objective, from Wave 1's cache), and a **\"what's happening\" line**\n223\t(most-recent lane activity / newest session title / its status). **Read caches only**\n224\ton render (no synchronous model call); generation stays the background-on-`rescan`\n225\tpath, and the existing `projects_html` in-place refresh updates the rows when a new\n226\tsummary lands. Honest placeholders when a project has no activity/summary yet.\n227\t\n228\t- **Done-when:** UI-verification set passes â€” each R&D project row shows its running\n229\t  count + latest objective summary + a recent-activity line, sourced from cache; a\n230\t  project mid-run shows it's active with its newest session; render performs no model\n231\t  call; rows refresh in place after a background summarize.\n232\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** a project with a running session and a cached objective summary,\n233\t  **When** the home dashboard renders, **Then** the row shows the objective + a\n234\t  \"running: N Â· latest: <session>\" reflection (cache only, no model call); **Given** a\n235\t  background `summarize_project` completes, **When** `projects_html` re-renders, **Then**\n236\t  the row updates in place.\n237\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_dashboard_reflection_v6.py` â€” DOM (row shows objective +\n238\t  activity line; positive+negative vs the v5 dot-only row) + render-path asserts no\n239\t  model call (cache only) + Playwright (row reflects a running stub session; in-place\n240\t  refresh) + screenshot.\n241\t\n242\t## Wave 8 â€” CLI mirror + healthcheck v6 + distro scan + docs (PROJECT DONE)\n243\t\n244\tMirror the new **read** seams into `anchor.py`: `rnd chain <pid> --session <id>`\n245\t(ordered chain members via `chain_members`), and ensure `rnd session-summary` /\n246\t`rnd build-deliverable` reflect the Wave 1 content. Extend `anchor_healthcheck.py`\n247\twith **`check_rnd_v6_surface`** (fully stubbed: stub PTY + stream-json stub runner +\n248\ttemp `ANCHOR_WORKTREE_BASE` + temp git project): walk (1) a summarizer round-trip\n249\tthrough the stream-json stub yields grounded non-empty session + project summaries +\n250\tschema-heal; (2) a chain â€” start research â†’ advance to planning (linked) â†’ finish\n251\tplanning-with-plan â†’ exactly-one auto build, asserting `chain_members`; (3) the\n252\ttiles/term_sessions projection includes terminal sessions and stays SAFE; tear\n253\teverything down (no `:8777`, no orphan PTY/worktree). Confirm `python -m distro` import\n254\tscan stays clean (Playwright NOT in product code). Update `CLAUDE.md` (a v6 \"Linked\n255\tPipeline\" section + new API rows: `advance_session`; CLI `rnd chain`; the new registry\n256\tfields + handoff stage edge; note Playwright is dev-only and UI waves are\n257\tPlaywright+screenshot+sign-off gated).\n258\t\n259\t- **Done-when:** the **full** suite GREEN; the new CLI subcommand works against the\n260\t  live registry; `check_rnd_v6_surface` passes fully stubbed + tears down (no `:8777`,\n261\t  no orphan PTY/worktree); `python -m distro` scan clean; `CLAUDE.md` documents v6.\n262\t- **G/W/T:** **Given** the stubbed env, **When** `check_rnd_v6_surface` runs, **Then**\n263\t  it walks summaries + the researchâ†’planâ†’build chain (incl. auto-advance + idempotency)\n264\t  and tears down with no orphan and never binds `:8777`; **and** the distro scan\n265\t  reports only the declared `pywinpty` exception (no Playwright in product code).\n266\t- **Tests:** `tests/test_cli_v6.py`, `tests/test_healthcheck_v6.py`,\n267\t  `tests/test_distro_scan_v6.py` â€” and the whole suite GREEN.\n268\t\n269\t## Project DONE\n270\t\n271\tDONE = Wave 8 GREEN on `python -m pytest -v` AND the Master Plan \"Definition of done\"\n272\tmet â€” including the UI waves' (3â€“7) Playwright + screenshot + **John's sign-off**.\n273\tTerminal wave = Wave 8. **No merge to master and no `nssm restart anchor` until John\n274\tsigns off** (then: merge, `nssm restart anchor` elevated, rescan each project to heal\n275\tsummaries).\n276\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"594fe9ce-c57e-43ec-93aa-7b0ba81bfc73","uuid":"62ec702d-4c27-4375-a15d-26357d35b46e","timestamp":"2026-06-15T12:19:05.407Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\planning\\rnd-v6\\IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md","content":"# Anchor R&D Surface v6 â€” \"Linked Pipeline\" â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n\n> Crucible Stage 2 output, locked 2026-06-14. Frozen design: `MASTER-PLAN.md` (this\n> folder) + the approved interaction mockup `_mockups/rnd-v6/session_pipeline.html`.\n> Build cwd = repo root `C:\\dev\\Anchor`, branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v6` (off master;\n> the summarizer parse fix `1bd8b85` is already cherry-picked as the branch base).\n> Each wave ends GREEN on the ground-truth gate and adds/extends tests under `tests/`.\n\ntest-command: python -m pytest -v\n\n## Conventions (read before any wave)\n\n- **Active Anchor project id:** read from `rnd_registry.json` at build time; never\n  hard-code (`2fe37f39â€¦` is retired; the live Anchor is the active one).\n- **No live `claude`/`gemini`/real-PTY in the gate.** Model calls via\n  `tests/fake_claude.py` / `tests/stub_streamjson.py` through `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`;\n  PTY via the stub backend (`ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`). Never `:8777` or real data;\n  any spawned preview/service on an OS-assigned port HARD-guarded `!= 8777` + isolated\n  temp `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`.\n- **pywinpty** is the only native dep (lazy, `pty_manager.py` only). **Playwright is a\n  DEV-ONLY test dep** â€” `pytest.importorskip(\"playwright.sync_api\")`; NEVER in product\n  code; `distro.py`'s scan must stay green (Wave 8 asserts it).\n- **f-string discipline** in `anchor_gui.py`: `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` is a RAW\n  single-brace string; double literal braces in f-string HTML/CSS.\n- **Security:** every new mutating / terminal / advance endpoint behind the existing\n  `do_POST` token gate; GET read-only (token via `?token=`).\n- **Reuse, don't fork:** build on `terminal_session.py`, `session_registry.py`,\n  `worktrees.py`, `handoff.py`, `summarizer.py`, `effort_history.py`, `job_runner.py`,\n  `pty_manager.py`, `report_viewer.py`, `vendor/xterm`.\n- **Scoped commits only** â€” never the runtime-data churn (`dashboard.html`,\n  `PROJECTS.md`, `DASHBOARD.md`, `domains/*`, `INBOX.md`, `.anchor/`, `rnd_jobs/`,\n  `rnd_registry.json`, `logs/`). Commit only the code/test files each wave touched.\n- **Baseline before Wave 1:** the v5 merge baseline was **643 passed, 1 skipped**;\n  the cherry-picked summarizer fix adds `tests/test_summary_streamjson.py`\n  (+ stub). Re-establish the live count at Wave 1 start; each wave must hold or grow it.\n- **UI VERIFICATION IS MANDATORY (the v4 lesson â€” non-negotiable)** for every wave\n  that changes rendered UI (Waves 3, 4, 5, 6, 7). \"GREEN\" requires ALL of: (a)\n  **rendered-DOM assertions** â€” parse the served HTML (style/script stripped) with\n  `html.parser`, assert the new structure present AND the replaced/old structure\n  absent (positive + negative); (b) a **real Playwright + Chromium interaction test**\n  (boot a throwaway `gui.make_server('127.0.0.1',0)`, click the actual control, assert\n  the resulting DOM + no JS console errors) â€” model on `tests/test_cockpit_paradigm2.py`\n  / `tests/test_run_lifecycle.py`; (c) the **orchestrator captures a screenshot**\n  (PNG under `_devtest/`), **Reads it**, and checks it against the rnd-v6 mockup; (d)\n  **user sign-off before merge**. A string-grep-only test is an automatic wave HALT.\n\n---\n\n## Wave 1 â€” Summaries that actually work (backend; lands the prod fix + content + heal)\n\nThe parse fix (`1bd8b85`) is already the branch base. This wave makes summaries\ngenuinely *informative* and *regression-proof*, and heals stale caches. Verify\n`summarizer.summarize_session` and `summarize_project` produce grounded, non-empty\ncontent when driven through a **stream-json-shaped** stub (`tests/stub_streamjson.py`),\nnot bare lines. Strengthen the **session** summary to convey skill Â· prompts/turns Â·\nactions/files and the **project** summary to convey objective/purpose (stronger seed:\nCLAUDE.md/README/Anchor.md + newest plan docs + pinned deliverables + per-lane\nactivity). Keep generate-twice + grounding filter (honest \"no grounded â€¦\" only when\ntruly absent; never fabricated). Ensure pre-fix caches (`SUMMARY_SCHEMA_VERSION` older/\nmissing) are treated as a MISS and **regenerate on rescan/force**. Add a small\n`rescan`-path helper (or confirm the existing background `summarize_project` on\n`rescan`) so existing empty project caches heal without manual force.\n\n- **Done-when:** `pytest` GREEN; through the stream-json stub, a session summary is\n  non-empty and carries skill/prompts/actions, and a project summary is a grounded\n  1â€“2 sentence objective; an ungrounded claim is dropped; a `SCHEMA_VERSION`-stale\n  empty cache is regenerated on rescan; bare-line stub back-compat still parses.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** a session/project whose runner emits `claude --output-format\n  stream-json` envelopes, **When** the summarizer runs through the stub, **Then** it\n  extracts the real text and caches a grounded, non-empty, informative summary;\n  **Given** a pre-fix empty `project-summary.json` (old/again missing schema version),\n  **When** the project is rescanned, **Then** the cache is treated as a miss and\n  regenerated (no longer \"No grounded objective\").\n- **Tests:** extend `tests/test_summary_streamjson.py`; add\n  `tests/test_summary_content_v6.py` (session skill/prompts/actions shape; project\n  objective shape; grounding drops a hallucinated claim; schema-version heal on\n  rescan). Backend only â€” no Playwright unless markup changes.\n\n## Wave 2 â€” Session linkage backbone (backend; the durable chain)\n\nGive sessions a durable lineage. Add `parent_session_id` (str|\"\") and `chain_id` (str)\nto the `session_registry` record (`_normalize` defaults + `register_session` params +\n`update_session` allow-list); a new session with no parent **starts its own chain**\n(`chain_id = session_id`), a child **inherits its parent's `chain_id`**. Add\n`session_registry.chain_for(session_id)` / `chain_members(chain_id)` (ordered\nresearchâ†’planâ†’build by lane then created_at) and a `terminal_session.start_session(...,\nparent_session_id=None)` passthrough that sets both fields. Extend `handoff.py` to\nrecord a **generic stage edge** (not just planâ†’build): a `record_stage_link(folder,\npid, from_session, to_session, kind)` appended to `discovery.json` (rescan-durable via\n`anchor_marker` merge, like existing handoffs), and have `discover_recent_plan_set`\nhonor an explicit `source_session_id` already (it does). No UI in this wave.\n\n- **Done-when:** `pytest` GREEN; a child session created with `parent_session_id`\n  inherits the parent's `chain_id`; `chain_members` returns the ordered chain; the\n  stage edge is persisted and **survives a registry reload + a rescan**; existing\n  records (no new fields) normalize with empty parent / self `chain_id` (back-compat).\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** a research session R, **When** a planning session P is started\n  with `parent_session_id=R`, **Then** P.chain_id == R.chain_id and\n  `chain_members(R.chain_id) == [R, P]` ordered; **When** the registry is reloaded and\n  the project rescanned, **Then** the Râ†’P edge and chain still resolve.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_session_chain.py` â€” field defaults/back-compat; chain\n  inherit + ordering; `chain_for`/`chain_members`; stage-edge persistence across\n  reload + rescan; `start_session(parent_session_id=â€¦)` through the stub PTY.\n\n## Wave 3 â€” First-class session windows: maximize + free resize (UI)\n\nIn `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` + the panel CSS: add a **maximize** control (â–¢) to each panel\nheader that toggles the panel to fill the cockpit viewport (`.panel.maxd`) and back,\nand make the panel **freely resizable** (drag any edge/corner â€” not just the terminal\nsub-pane), persisting size per session (extend `_panelHeights` â†’ `_panelRects`).\nKeep the v5 minimize, close-to-tile, and hard-kill exactly as they are; layout stays\nthe **stacked** column. Maximize/restore and resize MUST re-fit the xterm terminal\n(reuse the v4.1 fit + ResizeObserver) with no freeze and correct cols/rows.\n\n- **Done-when:** UI-verification set passes â€” every session panel has working\n  minimize / **maximize (toggle)** / **free resize** / close / kill; maximizing fills\n  the viewport and restores; resizing re-fits the terminal (correct cols/rows, no\n  freeze); the old \"terminal-pane-only vertical resize\" is no longer the only resize.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** an open session panel, **When** the user clicks maximize,\n  **Then** the panel fills the cockpit and the terminal re-fits; **When** clicked\n  again, **Then** it restores to its prior rect; **When** the user drags the panel's\n  corner, **Then** the panel resizes and the terminal re-fits with no console error.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_window_controls_v6.py` â€” DOM (maximize control present on\n  panels; resize affordance present; positive+negative vs the v5 header) + Playwright\n  (open panel â†’ maximize â†’ assert maxd geometry + terminal fit â†’ restore â†’ resize\n  drag â†’ assert new size, no JS console errors) + screenshot vs mockup Step 2.\n\n## Wave 4 â€” Tile lifecycle: new-session=new-tile + keep finished (newest-prominent) (UI)\n\nTwo fixes. (a) **Every start mints a tile:** audit every session-start front-end path\n(`newTermSession`, `continueSession`, `promoteGrass`, `developGrass`, and the new\nadvance paths) so each appends a distinct tile to the tiles row â€” none reuse/replace.\n(b) **Keep finished tiles, newest-prominent:** stop excluding terminal-status sessions\nfrom the tiles row (`repopulate`/`renderSessionBar` + the server `term_sessions`\nprojection) so done/failed sessions remain as **greyed, reopenable** tiles; per\nlane/chain render the **most-recent** session as the prominent tile and collapse older\nfinished ones under a **\"previously done\"** group/expander. Reopening a finished tile\nshows its summary panel (Wave 1); closing keeps the tile (v5); only hard-kill removes\nit.\n\n- **Done-when:** UI-verification set passes â€” starting any kind of session adds a new\n  tile; finishing a session keeps its tile (greyed) in the row without a reload; per\n  lane the newest is prominent and older finished ones are under \"previously done\";\n  reopening a finished tile opens its summary; kill removes the tile.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** the tiles row, **When** the user starts a second research\n  session, **Then** a second distinct research tile appears (the first is not\n  replaced); **When** a session finishes, **Then** its tile remains (greyed) and, if a\n  newer one exists in its lane, moves under \"previously done\"; **When** a finished tile\n  is clicked, **Then** its summary panel opens.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_tile_lifecycle_v6.py` â€” DOM (multiple same-lane tiles;\n  finished tile present + \"previously done\" group; positive+negative) + Playwright\n  (start two sessions â†’ two tiles; finish one â†’ still present + grouped; reopen â†’\n  summary) + backend (term_sessions projection now includes terminal sessions, still\n  SAFE â€” no worktree_path/branch).\n\n## Wave 5 â€” Manual advance researchâ†’planning + chain breadcrumb (UI + endpoint)\n\nAdd an **\"Advance to Planning â†’\"** control to a research session's window (shown when\nthe session looks done / on demand). It calls a new **`POST /api/rnd/advance_session`**\n(token-authed) â†’ `terminal_session.start_session(lane='planning',\nparent_session_id=<research>, seed_context=<research summary/report>)`, creating a NEW\nlinked planning tile seeded from the research; the research record is never mutated\n(reuses the v5 continue-seed builder). Render a **chain breadcrumb** (`R-1 â†’ P-2 â†’ â€¦`)\nin each session window header (and as a small affordance on the tile) from\n`chain_members`; clicking a breadcrumb node opens that session's panel. (This wave\nestablishes the generic advance endpoint that Wave 6 reuses for the auto path.)\n\n- **Done-when:** UI-verification set passes â€” a research window shows \"Advance to\n  Planning â†’\"; clicking it opens a new planning tile in the same chain, seeded from the\n  research, original intact; every linked session shows the chain breadcrumb and\n  clicking a node navigates the chain.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** a research session with a grounded summary, **When** the user\n  clicks \"Advance to Planning â†’\", **Then** a new RUNNING planning session starts in the\n  same `chain_id` with `parent_session_id` = the research and a seed containing the\n  research context, and the research record is unchanged; **When** the user clicks the\n  breadcrumb's research node from the planning window, **Then** the research panel opens.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_advance_research_to_plan.py` â€” endpoint auth + seeded-linked\n  start (new session, original intact, chain set) + DOM (advance control on research\n  only; breadcrumb present) + Playwright (click advance â†’ new planning tile + seed;\n  click breadcrumb â†’ navigates) + screenshot vs mockup Step 3.\n\n## Wave 6 â€” Auto advance planningâ†’build (gated on a real plan) (backend + UI)\n\nWhen a **planning** session reaches a terminal/**DONE** state â€” the deliberate\n**hard-kill** (\"done with planning\") or **reconcile-dead**, NOT a keep-alive close â€”\nthe server checks `handoff.discover_recent_plan_set(folder, pid,\nsource_session_id=<planning session>)`. If a **MASTER+IMPL plan set** is found, it\n**automatically** starts a NEW linked **build** session (`start_session(lane='build',\nparent_session_id=<planning>, â€¦)`), **primes** its worktree via\n`handoff.prime_worktree` (HANDOFF.md â†’ the plan docs) **before the planning worktree\nis reaped** (so the plan docs survive), and **records the stage edge** (Wave 2) â€”\nexactly one build per planning session (**idempotent** on `parent_session_id`, so\nreconcile/restart never duplicates). If **no** plan set is found, **no** advance. The\nnew build tile appears in the row (Wave 4), clearly attributed, even when the planning\nsession had no upstream research. Surface a tiny \"â†’ auto-opened Build B-n from this\nplan\" note. The trigger is the kill/reconcile-dead transition the cockpit already\nowns â€” never process self-exit, never a keep-alive close.\n\n- **Done-when:** UI-verification set passes â€” finishing a planning session that\n  produced a plan set auto-opens exactly one linked, primed build tile; a planning\n  session with no plan set opens none; the build is linked into the chain and survives\n  reconcile/restart without duplication; works with no upstream research.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** a planning session whose worktree contains a MASTER+IMPL plan\n  set, **When** it is hard-killed / found reconcile-dead (DONE transition), **Then**\n  the cockpit opens one build session with `parent_session_id` = the planning session,\n  a primed HANDOFF.md (referencing the real plan docs, captured before reap), and a\n  recorded stage edge; **Given** a planning session with no plan set, **When** it\n  finishes, **Then** no build is opened; **When** reconcile runs again, **Then** no\n  duplicate build is created; **When** a planning panel is keep-alive **closed**,\n  **Then** no build is opened (still live).\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_auto_advance_plan_to_build.py` â€” terminal-transition trigger\n  (stub PTY, temp git project with/without a plan set) â†’ exactly-one primed linked\n  build; idempotency across a second reconcile; no-plan â‡’ no-advance; no upstream\n  research path + DOM/Playwright (finishing a planning panel surfaces the new build\n  tile + note).\n\n## Wave 7 â€” Main dashboard reflects project activity (UI)\n\nUpgrade the home-dashboard R&D project rows (`render_project_tile_html` / the rows\nre-rendered by `GET /api/rnd/projects_html`) from a bare status dot to a **timely\nreflection**: per project show running-session presence/count, the **latest grounded\nproject summary** (objective, from Wave 1's cache), and a **\"what's happening\" line**\n(most-recent lane activity / newest session title / its status). **Read caches only**\non render (no synchronous model call); generation stays the background-on-`rescan`\npath, and the existing `projects_html` in-place refresh updates the rows when a new\nsummary lands. Honest placeholders when a project has no activity/summary yet.\n\n- **Done-when:** UI-verification set passes â€” each R&D project row shows its running\n  count + latest objective summary + a recent-activity line, sourced from cache; a\n  project mid-run shows it's active with its newest session; render performs no model\n  call; rows refresh in place after a background summarize.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** a project with a running session and a cached objective summary,\n  **When** the home dashboard renders, **Then** the row shows the objective + a\n  \"running: N Â· latest: <session>\" reflection (cache only, no model call); **Given** a\n  background `summarize_project` completes, **When** `projects_html` re-renders, **Then**\n  the row updates in place.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_dashboard_reflection_v6.py` â€” DOM (row shows objective +\n  activity line; positive+negative vs the v5 dot-only row) + render-path asserts no\n  model call (cache only) + Playwright (row reflects a running stub session; in-place\n  refresh) + screenshot.\n\n## Wave 8 â€” CLI mirror + healthcheck v6 + distro scan + docs (PROJECT DONE)\n\nMirror the new **read** seams into `anchor.py`: `rnd chain <pid> --session <id>`\n(ordered chain members via `chain_members`), and ensure `rnd session-summary` /\n`rnd build-deliverable` reflect the Wave 1 content. Extend `anchor_healthcheck.py`\nwith **`check_rnd_v6_surface`** (fully stubbed: stub PTY + stream-json stub runner +\ntemp `ANCHOR_WORKTREE_BASE` + temp git project): walk (1) a summarizer round-trip\nthrough the stream-json stub yields grounded non-empty session + project summaries +\nschema-heal; (2) a chain â€” start research â†’ advance to planning (linked) â†’ finish\nplanning-with-plan â†’ exactly-one auto build, asserting `chain_members`; (3) the\ntiles/term_sessions projection includes terminal sessions and stays SAFE; tear\neverything down (no `:8777`, no orphan PTY/worktree). Confirm `python -m distro` import\nscan stays clean (Playwright NOT in product code). Update `CLAUDE.md` (a v6 \"Linked\nPipeline\" section + new API rows: `advance_session`; CLI `rnd chain`; the new registry\nfields + handoff stage edge; note Playwright is dev-only and UI waves are\nPlaywright+screenshot+sign-off gated).\n\n- **Done-when:** the **full** suite GREEN; the new CLI subcommand works against the\n  live registry; `check_rnd_v6_surface` passes fully stubbed + tears down (no `:8777`,\n  no orphan PTY/worktree); `python -m distro` scan clean; `CLAUDE.md` documents v6.\n- **G/W/T:** **Given** the stubbed env, **When** `check_rnd_v6_surface` runs, **Then**\n  it walks summaries + the researchâ†’planâ†’build chain (incl. auto-advance + idempotency)\n  and tears down with no orphan and never binds `:8777`; **and** the distro scan\n  reports only the declared `pywinpty` exception (no Playwright in product code).\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_cli_v6.py`, `tests/test_healthcheck_v6.py`,\n  `tests/test_distro_scan_v6.py` â€” and the whole suite GREEN.\n\n## Project DONE\n\nDONE = Wave 8 GREEN on `python -m pytest -v` AND the Master Plan \"Definition of done\"\nmet â€” including the UI waves' (3â€“7) Playwright + screenshot + **John's sign-off**.\nTerminal wave = Wave 8. **No merge to master and no `nssm restart anchor` until John\nsigns off** (then: merge, `nssm restart anchor` elevated, rescan each project to heal\nsummaries).\n","numLines":276,"startLine":1,"totalLines":276}}}
